{"id":"330b7d77-4e7c-4a26-8e31-5a9d4cc1cbf1","object":"chat.completion","created":1795243404,"model":"deepseek-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"SELECT DATE_TRUNC('month', o.order_purchase_timestamp) AS month,\n       ROUND(AVG(t.order_amount), 2) AS avg_order_items_amount\nFROM (\n  SELECT o.order_id,\n         DATE_TRUNC('month', o.order_purchase_timestamp) AS month,\n         SUM(oi.price) AS order_amount\n  FROM orders o\n  JOIN order_items oi ON oi.order_id = o.order_id\n  GROUP BY o.order_id, DATE_TRUNC('month', o.order_purchase_timestamp)\n) t\nGROUP BY month\nORDER BY month\nLIMIT 1000;","reasoning_content":"We need answer only SQL, no fences, one SELECT, must follow schema. Need parse Chinese question carefully.\n\n\"每个有商品明细的月份，按有商品明细的订单等权，计算每单明细商品金额合计的平均值；无明细订单不参与均值。\"\n\nWe need compute per month (based on orders? \"有商品明细的月份\" likely months with order items; use order_purchase_timestamp? Need decide) For each month with item details, treat orders with item details equally, calculate average over orders of sum of order item price (商品金额合计). Orders without details excluded. Need output month and average amount. Need group by month, aggregate per order first sum(oi.price), then average across orders. Use orders for purchase timestamp and order_id. Start order_items joined orders. Need probably use DATE_TRUNC('month', o.order_purchase_timestamp) as month. Need ensure only months with item details. Order with items included once. We can do subquery at order-month level: SELECT DATE_TRUNC('month', o.order_purchase_timestamp) AS month, o.order_id, SUM(oi.price) AS order_items_amount FROM orders o JOIN order_items oi ON oi.order_id=o.order_id GROUP BY 1,o.order_id. Then outer SELECT month, ROUND(AVG(order_items_amount),2) AS avg_order_amount FROM (...) t GROUP BY month ORDER BY month. Need consider month could have multiple orders, AVG numeric. Need maybe alias. Need only one SELECT. Use month maybe need year-month? The question \"每个有商品明细的月份\" output month. Default for month grouping uses DATE_TRUNC('month', 时间列), per rule. Could use DATE_TRUNC('month', o.order_purchase_timestamp) maybe timestamp. Need maybe cast? no requirement. We can use DATE_TRUNC('month', o.order_purchase_timestamp) AS month. Need include months with items. No filter beyond join. Orders without detail excluded. \"每单明细商品金额合计\" = order_items.price sum per order. \"按有商品明细的订单等权\" means each order equal weight, not each item. So pre-aggregate per order and average.\n\nNeed watch order_items composite PK, but each row unique by order_id/order_item_id. SUM price per order. If order has multiple items. No duplicate due join. Good.\n\nNeed ensure no additional filter approved etc. Not.\n\nNeed output maybe average rounded 2 due money. The question doesn't explicitly state formatting. For average amount, money maybe round 2. Rule: 金额/单价/均值 ROUND two. It says \"其余金额/单价/均值 ROUND两位\". Use ROUND(AVG(order_amount), 2). Since AVG returns numeric from numeric sum, okay.\n\nCould use CTE? Only one SELECT, CTE acceptable? It says only one SELECT perhaps no WITH? Better use subquery.\n\nNeed final only SQL. Use semicolon? fine.\n\nLet's formulate:\n\nSELECT DATE_TRUNC('month', o.order_purchase_timestamp) AS month,\n       ROUND(AVG(t.order_amount), 2) AS avg_order_amount\nFROM (\n  SELECT o.order_id, DATE_TRUNC('month', o.order_purchase_timestamp) AS month, SUM(oi.price) AS order_amount\n  FROM orders o\n  JOIN order_items oi ON oi.order_id = o.order_id\n  GROUP BY o.order_id, DATE_TRUNC('month', o.order_purchase_timestamp)\n) t\nGROUP BY month\nORDER BY month;\n\nNeed include limit? Query grouped returns many rows (months ~ maybe 20). Rule must LIMIT unless single-row aggregate. Here grouped by month, needs LIMIT? It says must LIMIT, single-line no GROUP BY aggregate except. We have GROUP BY, so need LIMIT. But adding LIMIT arbitrary? The query asks each month, should return all months. But hard rule 3 says must LIMIT. Need add LIMIT maybe 100 or number enough. But output all? In schema range ~2 years, months ~26. Could add LIMIT 100 maybe avoids missing? Yet the question \"每个有商品明细的月份\" expects all. Hard rule demands LIMIT. Could add LIMIT 1000. But if more, fails. In this dataset max ~26. Use LIMIT 1000. But maybe \"每个...\" means all, LIMIT could violate? System says must LIMIT; can add LIMIT 1000. It won't truncate for data. Fine.\n\nNeed check \"有商品明细的月份\" month from what? Could use order purchase timestamp. Maybe order_items no timestamp. Yes use orders.order_purchase_timestamp. Could use shipping_limit_date? No. Business month of order purchase.\n\nPotential issue orders rows with no item excluded. Good.\n\nCould use ROUND(AVG(t.order_amount), 2) AS average_order_items_amount. Fine.\n\nNeed no explanations. Final only SQL."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":3042,"completion_tokens":1164,"total_tokens":4206,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":2816},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1035},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":2816,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":226},"system_fingerprint":"bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}